WEBVTT

00:00:01.588 --> 00:00:11.992
The last one: AI part design. Menu “AI Parts → AI part design…”

00:00:11.992 --> 00:00:22.417
Choose the part type (stepped shaft), then write the requirement: speed, motor, mechanism data, axial positions, material… the bearing model can be left open

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:28.967
Click “Load example: Sewing machine upper shaft”: a ready-written requirement (illustrative data; in Chinese, because the recorded AI replies are for this text)

00:00:28.967 --> 00:00:40.967
It asks for: 5000 r/min, able to go to 5500; bearing centres at 27 and 252 mm; where the crank, cam, eccentric, pulley and handwheel sit and what they weigh; steel 45 quenched and tempered, safety factor 1.5, bearing life 20,000 hours

00:00:44.493 --> 00:00:51.181
Click “Start design”. The AI replies are recordings of a real model; the panel says so

00:00:51.181 --> 00:00:58.968
Result: all passed, 4 rounds. How? AI lists the conditions and proposes designs; whether they work is computed by code

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:08.367
“Conditions”: the speeds, bearing positions, loads and masses AI read from the text, each checked against the original words

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:16.942
“AI questions”: where the text is unclear, AI does not guess but asks — for example whether bearing life is at 5000 or 5500 r/min

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:21.967
“Rounds”: round 1 passes, but the shaft is Ø46 and 3.55 kg

00:01:21.967 --> 00:01:31.318
Every item is checked by code: whether the bearings slide on, shoulder heights, the safety factor at every step, critical speed, bearing life

00:01:31.318 --> 00:01:40.992
After it passes, it goes back to AI to lose weight and is checked again; round 4 is 0.28 kg and still passes — the lightest passing round is used

00:01:40.992 --> 00:01:52.468
Then the 3D model and drawing are made, and the sizes are read back from the model and compared with the design segment by segment; the drawing comes out only if they match

00:01:52.468 --> 00:02:04.468
At the bottom, “Confirm into enterprise library”: in real use the engineer fills in the drawing number and their name, and only then does it go in; a replayed example cannot, so the button is grey

00:02:05.543 --> 00:02:17.543
All three in this lesson — choosing parts, the parts library, designing a part — follow the same rule: AI drafts, code checks, a person decides. That is the end of the course
